-- title:
--   An anharmonic automorphism transporting level-two nodes over j=0,1728
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism, and let $a\in k$ satisfy $a=0$ or $a=1728$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, write $A_0:=A\cap K$ for `coeffSubring A K` and $\rho:=$ `redRestrict red K` for the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$, and let $y_1,y_2\in A_0$ satisfy, with $\ell_i:=\rho(y_i)$, the relations $a\bigl((16\ell_i)^2(16\ell_i-1)^2\bigr)=256\bigl((16\ell_i)^2-16\ell_i+1\bigr)^3$ for $i=1,2$. Let $L:=$ `lambdaFieldOver q K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series attached to $K$ together with $\lambda$ and its $q$-fold $q$-expansion $\lambda_q$. Then there is a ring automorphism $\sigma$ of $L$ such that: (i) $\sigma$ fixes every element of $L$ whose underlying Laurent series lies in the image, under the substitution $\mathfrak q\mapsto\mathfrak q^{2}$, of the subfield generated by the constant series attached to $K$ together with $j$ and its $q$-fold $q$-expansion; and (ii) for every subring $B$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ contained in $L$ which contains $p(\lambda,\lambda_q)$ for every $p\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ (the homomorphism `lambdaEval`) and is mapped into itself by $\sigma$, and every ideal $I$ of $B$: if $p(\lambda,\lambda_q)\in I$ for all $p$ with $\bar p(\ell_1,\ell_1^{\,q})=0$ (coefficients reduced by $\rho$, the homomorphism `pointEval`), then $\sigma\bigl(p(\lambda,\lambda_q)\bigr)\in I$ for all $p$ with $\bar p(\ell_2,\ell_2^{\,q})=0$.
--
--   This is the transitivity of the anharmonic group of the $\lambda$-line on the level-two points lying over a point of the $j$-line with $j=0$ or $j=1728$, in the form needed for nodes of the level-$q$ modular correspondence: one of the six anharmonic substitutions, applied simultaneously to $\lambda$ and to $\lambda_q$, fixes the level-one field and carries the vanishing ideal of the first node into that of the second. It is used in the identification of the prime ideals of the descended node ring lying over such a $j$-value, [`ModularCurve.eq_of_isPrime_of_liesOver_descendedNodeRing_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eq_of_isPrime_of_liesOver_descendedNodeRing_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728).
